Subject: Crack indications on NR-21-L-0412 - line out of service
Message-ID: <9d10b9849103563b30437870@qscp.example.invalid>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8

Dear Daniel,

Following the removal of wet insulation on NR-21-L-0412 in ANLAGE-21, penetrant testing has confirmed the presence of branched crack indications at three separate locations. According to RLW-PB-2014-0098, these indications were identified under areas of damaged cladding that had been noted as a deficiency since 2013. As crack indications are always unzulässig under our site rules, we have issued NR-AB-2014-03 to document this nonconformity.

Due to the risk of external chloride-induced stress corrosion cracking on this 1.4404 line, NR-21-L-0412 has been taken out of service immediately. We will need to evaluate repair options or replacement before the line can be returned to operation.

Best regards,  Thomas Brüggemann Prüfkoordinator QSCP Deutschland GmbH, Werk Niederrhein  Recipient: Daniel Hartmann, QSCP Corporate Asset Integrity

